---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../../../components/Hero.astro";
import Figure from "../../../components/Figure.astro";
import Icon from "../../../components/Icon.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../../consts";
import heroImg from "../../../assets/photos/tokyo-evo9-arriere-onlyjdm.jpg";
import mapImg from "../../../assets/photos/tokyo-onlyjdm-itineraire-shinjuku.webp";
import avantImg from "../../../assets/photos/tokyo-evo9-avant-rue-onlyjdm.jpg";
import volantImg from "../../../assets/photos/tokyo-evo9-interieur-volant-onlyjdm.jpg";

const agencyName = "OnlyJDM Car Rental Haneda Airport Store";
const agencyAddress = "〒143-0013 Tokyo, Ota City, Omoriminami, 2 Chome-20-14";
const mapsHref = `https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=${encodeURIComponent(`${agencyName}, ${agencyAddress}`)}`;
---

<Layout
  title="OnlyJDM"
  description="OnlyJDM in Tokyo: a JDM rental specialist worth the trip for any enthusiast. Requirements, prices, getting there and my full review."
>
  <Hero
    image={heroImg}
    eyebrow="Great spot · Tokyo"
    title="OnlyJDM"
    subtitle="The pros and cons: I'll tell you everything!"
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-10 sm:pt-14 pb-8 sm:pb-10 sm:px-8">
    <a
      href={withBase("/en/tokyo/")}
      class="link-underline reveal inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-ink-soft"
    >
      <Icon name="arrow-left" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      Back to Tokyo
    </a>

    <p class="reveal mt-8 font-body text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      A bit of backstory: a month before leaving for Japan, I had no idea you could rent JDM cars. After several days
      of research, especially on how to rent and how to get my license translated, I found this agency called
      OnlyJDM. This is where I picked up the keys to this Lancer Evolution VIII. Looks great, doesn't it? :) Modified
      exhaust, upgraded turbo, new steering wheel and wheels: it's pretty far from the stock version, which I don't
      mind one bit.
    </p>
    <p class="reveal mt-4 font-body text-xs text-mist-500">Not sponsored: I paid for the rental myself.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-8 sm:pb-10 sm:px-8">
    <h2 class="reveal font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Requirements to rent</h2>
    <p class="reveal mt-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Before picking up your car at this agency or any other, here's what you'll need:
    </p>
    <ul class="reveal mt-4 space-y-2 border-l-2 border-mist-200 pl-5 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      <li>Be at least 23 years old (the age required at OnlyJDM, it may vary from one agency to another)</li>
      <li>
        Your printed license translation, or your International Driving Permit depending on your country (learn more:{" "}
        <a href={withBase("/en/driving-in-japan/")} class="link-underline font-medium text-racing-500">Driving in Japan</a>)
      </li>
      <li>Your physical driver's license (no paper version allowed)</li>
      <li>Your passport</li>
      <li>
        Cash or a credit card to pay the deposit (between €200 and €300 depending on the car), and for souvenirs
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-8 sm:pb-10 sm:px-8">
    <h2 class="reveal font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Why OnlyJDM?</h2>
    <div class="reveal mt-4 space-y-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      <p>OnlyJDM lets you rent any car you want, depending on availability.</p>
      <p>
        I chose this agency for its attractive prices compared to other agencies, which can sometimes charge you €100
        more, or even more than that, for less driving time. Here you can rent for 7 hours or 24 hours (count on about
        3,000 yen more, around €17: it's better value and lets you drive at night).
      </p>
      <p>
        As for availability: some cars get booked up fast, so it's really essential to book quickly and to already
        have your license translation, or plan for it in advance.
      </p>
      <p>They have 2 agencies:</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 border-l-2 border-mist-200 pl-5">
        <li>one in the north of Tokyo (hard to reach by public transport)</li>
        <li>one in the south of Tokyo (easier to get to)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>I booked the EVO 8 GSR from the southern agency.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-10 sm:pb-14 sm:px-8">
    <h2 class="reveal font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">How to get there?</h2>

    <div class="reveal mt-6 rounded-lg border border-mist-200 bg-paper-dim/40 p-5">
      <p class="eyebrow text-racing-500">The agency's address</p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-body text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{agencyName}</p>
      <p class="mt-1 flex items-start gap-1.5 font-body text-sm text-ink-soft">
        <Icon name="map-pin" class="mt-0.5 h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0 text-mist-500" />
        Japan, {agencyAddress}
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
        <a
          href={mapsHref}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link-underline inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-racing-500"
        >
          Open in Google Maps
          <Icon name="external-link" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://only-jdm.com/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link-underline inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-racing-500"
        >
          Agency website
          <Icon name="external-link" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <Figure
      image={mapImg}
      alt="Map of the train route between Shinjuku Station and the OnlyJDM agency in south Tokyo"
      caption="Route from Shinjuku Station, Google Maps screenshot."
      class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-md"
    />

    <div class="reveal mt-8 space-y-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      <p>
        Since I was staying in Shinjuku, it took me about 40 minutes by regional train plus a 15-minute walk to reach
        the agency. I know it's a long trip unless you're willing to spend about €60 on a taxi (about 30 minutes by
        road). Add that to the car rental and the gas (about €1 per liter), and it can add up quickly, but the reward
        will be all the sweeter!
      </p>
      <p>
        To get around, I recommend having a 5G SIM card and Google Maps: from your hotel, it'll give you the best route
        in detail (which platform, which direction, which train, etc.).
      </p>
      <p>
        Don't be late! The agency is usually open before your rental starts, so it's best to allow for transport
        hiccups.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before picking up your car, read the contract carefully, take photos and videos of the car in case of any
        problem, and let your heart choose! In short, just like at any regular rental agency.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="reveal mt-8 font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">What's next? Enjoy it!</p>
    <div class="reveal mt-4 space-y-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      <p>
        My experience was unforgettable, even though the rain really made its presence felt during the drive. Driving
        through the streets of Tokyo, especially Shibuya at night and the little streets of Kabukicho, definitely left
        an impression on me!
      </p>
      <p>
        A quick run on the expressway over the Rainbow Bridge, with the engine singing, is a real treat, especially
        knowing that in Japan, car modifications are still tolerated. It wouldn't be the same experience in France...
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <Figure
        image={avantImg}
        alt="Front of the gray Lancer Evolution VIII parked along a sidewalk in a Tokyo street"
        caption="The front of the Mitsubishi"
        class="text-center"
        aspectClass="aspect-[3/4]"
      />
      <Figure
        image={volantImg}
        alt="Driver's seat of the Lancer Evolution VIII with an aftermarket sport steering wheel"
        caption="Now that's a steering wheel!"
        class="text-center"
        aspectClass="aspect-[3/4]"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-mist-200 bg-paper-dim/50 py-10 sm:py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 text-center sm:px-8">
      <a
        href={withBase("/en/tokyo/")}
        class="link-underline reveal inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-ink"
      >
        <Icon name="arrow-left" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
        Back to all Tokyo spots
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
